{"content":[{"id":"68e869db","settings":{"background_background":"classic","__globals__":{"background_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","background_overlay_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"},"padding":{"unit":"px","top":"100","right":"0","bottom":"100","left":"0","isLinked":false},"background_image":{"url":"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/hero-neighborhood_25.webp","id":233193,"size":"","alt":"","source":"library"},"background_position":"center center","background_repeat":"no-repeat","background_size":"cover","background_overlay_background":"classic","background_overlay_opacity":{"unit":"px","size":0.80000000000000004,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[{"id":"1327306f","settings":{"content_width":"full","flex_direction":"row","flex_align_items":"center"},"elements":[{"id":"5658f452","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"6c012084","settings":{"title":"Air Conditioning Repair in Louisburg, NC\n","header_size":"h1","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","typography_typography":""},"typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Ruda","typography_font_size":{"unit":"em","size":3,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"em","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":"","sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"bold","title_color":"#FFFFFF"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"62ebb3a9","settings":{"title":"AC Repair for Homes and Businesses Across the Louisburg Area","header_size":"p","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","typography_typography":"globals\/typography?id=b279f6f"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3a4a35a8","settings":{"editor":"<p>In Louisburg and nearby North Carolina communities, AC problems can get worse quickly once heat and humidity settle in. If your air conditioner stops cooling, starts making strange noises, leaks water, or struggles to keep up, even a small issue can affect comfort, energy bills, airflow, and system reliability.<\/p><p>Dolan Design HVAC &amp; Plumbing provides dependable air conditioning repair for residential and commercial properties across Louisburg, Raleigh, Wake Forest, Zebulon, Youngsville, and nearby North Carolina communities.<\/p><p>Our team helps you understand what is wrong, what can be repaired, and what steps make the most sense for your comfort, system performance, and budget.<\/p>","__globals__":{"text_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2b44d246","settings":{"text":"Request Service Online","link":{"url":"#contact","is_external":"","nofollow":"","custom_attributes":""},"border_border":"solid","border_width":{"unit":"px","top":"1","right":"1","bottom":"1","left":"1","isLinked":true},"border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"button_text_color":"globals\/colors?id=be5c055","border_color":"globals\/colors?id=be5c055"},"selected_icon":{"value":"far fa-arrow-alt-circle-right","library":"fa-regular"},"icon_align":"row-reverse","align":"left"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"button","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"17da1d0f","settings":{"flex_direction":"column","background_background":"classic","background_color":"#EDF4FF","__globals__":{"background_color":""}},"elements":[{"id":"57fa8beb","settings":{"content_width":"full","flex_direction":"row","flex_align_items":"center"},"elements":[{"id":"28dca1d8","settings":{"content_width":"full","padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true}},"elements":[{"id":"422e777f","settings":{"title":"Signs You May Need Air Conditioning Repair\n","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=text","typography_typography":"globals\/typography?id=7549918"},"title_color":"#FFFFFF"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1e5de6a6","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Not every AC problem means your system is failing completely. In many cases, timely repair can restore comfort, improve efficiency, and help prevent more expensive damage.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You may need air conditioning repair if you notice:<\/span><\/p>","__globals__":{"text_color":"globals\/colors?id=text"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"208a2974","settings":{"content_width":"full","flex_direction":"row","padding":{"unit":"px","top":"0","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":true},"container_type":"grid","grid_columns_grid":{"unit":"fr","size":2,"sizes":[]},"grid_rows_grid":{"unit":"fr","size":0,"sizes":[]},"presetTitle":"Grid","presetIcon":"eicon-container-grid"},"elements":[{"id":"5a9270b8","settings":{"icon_list":[{"text":"Your AC is blowing warm air","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"485fdfd"},{"text":"Airflow feels weak from the vents","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"4b13f9c"},{"text":"Rooms cool unevenly","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"dce6075"},{"text":"The system turns on and off frequently","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"3ad1de2"},{"text":"Energy bills are rising without a clear reason","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"3ea29a4"},{"text":"The outdoor unit will not start","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"96adf10"},{"text":"Your thermostat is not responding correctly","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"73f63be"}],"space_between":{"unit":"px","size":5,"sizes":[]},"icon_color":"#FAB914","icon_size":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"icon_typography_typography":"custom","icon_typography_font_family":"Ruda","icon_typography_font_size":{"unit":"em","size":0.90000000000000002,"sizes":[]},"icon_typography_font_weight":"400","text_color":"#222222","icon_typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"em","size":"","sizes":[]},"icon_typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":"","sizes":[]},"__globals__":{"text_color":"globals\/colors?id=text","icon_typography_typography":""}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-list","elType":"widget"},{"id":"70ac1a5a","settings":{"icon_list":[{"text":"The system makes grinding, buzzing, rattling, or squealing noises","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"2e6b785"},{"text":"Water is leaking around the indoor unit","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"c4adebb"},{"text":"Ice forms on the evaporator coil","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"dd63fed"},{"text":"Your AC gives off musty, burning, or unusual smells","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"e8cbf06"},{"text":"Breakers trip when the system runs","selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"_id":"8b5659b"}],"space_between":{"unit":"px","size":5,"sizes":[]},"icon_color":"#FAB914","icon_size":{"unit":"px","size":18,"sizes":[]},"icon_typography_typography":"custom","icon_typography_font_family":"Ruda","icon_typography_font_size":{"unit":"em","size":0.90000000000000002,"sizes":[]},"icon_typography_font_weight":"400","text_color":"#222222","icon_typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"em","size":"","sizes":[]},"icon_typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":"","sizes":[]},"__globals__":{"text_color":"globals\/colors?id=text","icon_typography_typography":""}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-list","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"},{"id":"716d6b5e","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A cooling system does not have to stop working completely to need attention. If your AC is running but comfort is slipping, a professional inspection can help identify the issue before it turns into a larger breakdown.<\/span><\/p>","__globals__":{"text_color":"globals\/colors?id=text"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"},{"id":"35d7e3e","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"38d96715","settings":{"image":{"url":"https:\/\/dolandesignhvac.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/06\/techician-servicing-ac-uni-outsidet.jpg","id":233248,"size":"","alt":"Signs You May Need Air Conditioning Repair","source":"library"},"height":{"unit":"px","size":550,"sizes":[]},"object-fit":"cover","image_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"height_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":300,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"image","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"4b0917b9","settings":{"flex_direction":"column"},"elements":[{"id":"733038a1","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"25092192","settings":{"title":"Common AC Repair Issues We Diagnose\n","align":"center","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=text"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3ae8156","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Every property has different cooling needs, but many AC repair calls start with familiar symptoms. A proper diagnosis helps determine whether the issue is minor, mechanical, electrical, airflow-related, or tied to the age of the system.<\/span><\/p>","align":"center"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"},{"id":"28f7f4a6","settings":{"content_width":"full","container_type":"grid","presetTitle":"Grid","presetIcon":"eicon-container-grid"},"elements":[{"id":"48765d96","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"title_text":"Refrigerant Leaks","description_text":"Low refrigerant can cause warm air, poor cooling, frozen coils, and longer run times. If refrigerant is low, the leak should be located and repaired before the system is recharged.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3dc29bd0","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"title_text":"Frozen Evaporator Coils","description_text":"Frozen coils are often caused by restricted airflow, dirty filters, low refrigerant, or dirty coils. If ignored, this can reduce cooling performance and place stress on other components.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"57bb19b6","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"title_text":"Thermostat Problems","description_text":"A faulty or poorly calibrated thermostat can cause inaccurate temperature readings, short cycling, delayed cooling, or a system that will not turn on or off properly.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"d00cfba","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"title_text":"Capacitor and Electrical Issues","description_text":"Capacitors, contactors, relays, and electrical connections help your AC start and run safely. When these parts fail, you may hear clicking or buzzing, experience breaker trips, or find that the system will not start.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"23a88edc","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"title_text":"Compressor and Fan Motor Problems","description_text":"The compressor and fan motors are critical to cooling performance. When they begin to fail, you may notice loud operation, weak cooling, warm air, frequent shutdowns, or an outdoor unit that struggles to run.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"40e2c016","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"title_text":"Ductwork and Airflow Problems","description_text":"Not every cooling issue starts inside the AC unit itself. Leaky ducts, blocked vents, dirty filters, or blower motor problems can reduce airflow and make certain rooms harder to cool.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"50adbc41","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"title_text":"Drain Line and Moisture Problems","description_text":"A clogged condensate drain line can cause water to back up into the system or leak around the indoor unit. Addressing drainage problems early helps prevent water damage, mold growth, and system shutdowns.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"5a112fbf","settings":{"flex_direction":"column"},"elements":[{"id":"439899f0","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"1ec599d7","settings":{"title":"Our AC Repair Process\n","align":"center","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=text"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6220afac","settings":{"editor":"<p>A good AC repair starts with understanding the full picture. Dolan Design HVAC &amp; Plumbing follows a clear process to help make the experience straightforward.<\/p>","align":"center","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"globals\/typography?id=b279f6f"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"},{"id":"5b5cfafb","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"406b03ad","settings":{"content_width":"full","container_type":"grid","grid_align_items":"start","background_background":"classic","border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"padding":{"unit":"px","top":"15","right":"15","bottom":"15","left":"15","isLinked":true},"presetTitle":"Grid","presetIcon":"eicon-container-grid","__globals__":{"background_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[{"id":"63aa9a53","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-1","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"System Evaluation","description_text":"We inspect your current cooling system, listen to your concerns, and look for obvious signs of failure, wear, airflow issues, or electrical trouble.\n","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2ce22efb","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-2","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Comfort and Airflow Review","description_text":"We check weak airflow, hot spots, humidity concerns, thermostat operation, filter condition, and ductwork-related symptoms that may affect cooling performance.","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3c9f14fe","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-3","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Repair Recommendations","description_text":"Our team explains the issue, recommended repairs, urgency level, available options, and any cost considerations before work begins.","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"69e77f2c","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-4","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Professional Repair","description_text":"Once you approve the recommended repair, we address the issue with attention to system safety, performance, airflow, drainage, and reliable operation.","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6701d9e5","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-5","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Final Testing and Walkthrough","description_text":"Before leaving, we test the system, verify cooling performance, answer questions, and explain next steps. Many repairs are completed the same visit.","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"},{"id":"a4520d1","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"342742a","settings":{"editor":"<p>For many standard replacements, the work can often be completed in one day. More complex projects may take longer if ductwork, electrical updates, or accessibility issues need to be addressed.<\/p>","align":"center","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Ruda","typography_font_weight":"bold","_element_width":"initial","_element_custom_width":{"unit":"%","size":70,"sizes":[]},"_flex_align_self":"center","_element_custom_width_mobile":{"unit":"%","size":100,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"3e7bb