item_title":"Do you repair AC systems for commercial properties?","_id":"b44da10"},{"item_title":"What should I do before calling for AC repair?","_id":"853f04c"}]},"elements":[{"id":"1cb631ce","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"29b9d899","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Warm air may be caused by low refrigerant, a refrigerant leak, dirty coils, thermostat issues, compressor problems, or restricted airflow. A technician can identify the cause and recommend the right repair.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"6b081f92","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"531badaf","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Frequent cycling can point to thermostat problems, airflow restrictions, electrical issues, refrigerant problems, or an improperly sized system. Short cycling should be checked because it can increase wear and energy use.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"1c8f362f","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"475af393","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It can be. Water near the indoor unit may come from a clogged condensate drain line, damaged drain pan, frozen coil, or drainage issue. Left alone, it can cause moisture damage or system shutdowns.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"a8dc012","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"13228a08","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Repair may make sense if the system is newer, the issue is minor, cooling performance is still reliable, and energy bills are stable. Replacement may be worth considering if the system is older, repairs are frequent, repair costs are high, major components are failing, or comfort and efficiency keep declining.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"62f3df72","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"797517ec","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. If your system is running inefficiently because of dirty coils, weak airflow, low refrigerant, failing electrical parts, or thermostat issues, the right repair may help reduce unnecessary runtime and energy waste.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"244b5d60","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"6a79b52d","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. Dolan Design HVAC &amp; Plumbing provides AC repair for both residential and commercial properties in Louisburg and nearby North Carolina communities.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"50cfb344","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"fbaadd9","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Check your thermostat settings, replace or inspect the air filter, make sure breakers are not tripped, and confirm vents are open. If the system still is not working properly, schedule service.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true}],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"nested-accordion","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"12d591c1","settings":{"flex_di